# Minimal Comments

Do not add comments unless absolutely necessary. Comments should explain non-obvious intent, trade-offs, or constraints the code cannot convey on its own. Never narrate what the code plainly does.

Delete/avoid clutter comments like this:

```liquid
{% comment %} Match the JS card slot width: 1200px section width divided by columns per row {% endcomment %}
```

Guidelines:
- No comments that restate the code (e.g. `// increment counter`, `// import module`).
- No TODO/placeholder comments promising future work.
- Prefer clear names over explanatory comments.
- When a comment is genuinely warranted, keep it to one concise line explaining *why*, not *what*.
